WEBVTT

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.090
Those claw marks!

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.960
You're joking, right?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.300
The Legitimate Heir's Kekkai
can't be this weak.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.100
Shishio Gen from the Night Troops,
Special Forces of the Shadow Organization.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.210
Dispatched to provide security

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.980
to the Karasumori Site
and assist the Kekkaishi here.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.380
Tokine!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.120
Let's chase him out!

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.620
Both of you... are way too slow.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.860
You're here to assist us Kekkaishi, right?

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.630
Then you shouldn't be doing things
without our permission.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.900
Kekkaishi. huh?

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.530
As far as I know

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.700
Kekkaishi are the most
powerful Casters in existence.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.140
But you're completely different.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.210
While these two continue to be
at each other's throats.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:04.920
a new enemy's invasion has
begun... slowly.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.090
Junior high student Sumimura Yoshimori
and high school student Yukimura Tokine

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.690
protect the Karasumori Site, where
the school now stands, from the Ayakashi.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:19.440
It is their ancestral duty as Kekkaishi.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.810
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.680
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.890
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.790
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:38.230
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:42.630
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.170
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.500
I will protect you that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.170
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.670
Sha la la la la...

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:06.090
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.060
(Secret romance)

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.260
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.020
(A strange distance)

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.870
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:22.940
Yeah

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:26.410
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.010
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:35.350
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.530
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.800
Yoshimori, you're getting too worked up!

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:07.970
Shut up!

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.350
You're slow as always.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.550
Why you-!

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.260
Wait!

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.690
We have to clean this up first.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.330
Ketsu!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.530
Metsu!

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.410
Are you okay with this?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.550
Letting him go around and
do whatever he wants?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.910
Whatever he wants?
He's just doing his job.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:49.350
You should stop complaining
and help me clean this up.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.300
W-What?! You make it sound
like we're his assistants!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.660
Do you know how many times
we've had to clean up after him?!

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:02.790
It's the eighth time
he's gotten the jump on you.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.940
Shut up, you ghost dog!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.500
You asked!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.100
I didn't ask that!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.870
You should thank me
for keeping count!

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.810
Why don't you try to learn
from this experience?!

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.140
Shut up! If only you were reliable!

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.240
Don't blame me for your incompetence!

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.580
Who're you calling incompetent?

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.680
Yoshi looks really irritated.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.090
He won't be able to use his techniques
properly with his mind in that state.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.860
Man, he never grows up.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.000
You don't look happy
about this either, honey.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.970
I. uh...

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.900
It's true we can't let
it stay like this.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.680
Maybe I should try talking to
Gen-kun tomorrow.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.810
How's it going lately?

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.540
Not very well.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.210
Oh.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.730
They seem to hate each other a lot.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.860
That look in his eyes...
doesn't it seem dangerous?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.990
Like he could attack any moment.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.330
We'll probably be fine about
80 to 90 percent of the time.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.140
What about the other 10 to 20 percent?

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.000
You sure you want to know?

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.010
I. uh... never mind.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.440
H-Hiba-san!

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.830
Hey, wake up.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.770
Am I that unreliable?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.610
I'm not like the chief.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.120
I'm a member of
the Night Troops.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.350
I'll live up to
the Chief's expectations.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:05.720
Besides...

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.290
I think you're misunderstanding something.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.270
There's only one thing you must adhere to.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:13.930
I know.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.500
To restrain myself.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.110
Either I hit him from behind
with a Kekkai

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:25.340
or bind him up with my Nenshi...

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.110
Come on.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:28.340
I know.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.780
I have to beat him fair and square!

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.290
Ow. What was that for? Stop it!

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.020
You need to chill out.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.990
I understand you don't like him.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.890
But don't you have more
important goals in mind?

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.130
W-Well...

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.700
He keeps comparing me
to my older brother.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.800
That really annoys me.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.470
Gen-kun.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.540
I want to talk to you.
Do you have a minute?

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.080
Hey!

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.620
What's his problem?
Why is he ignoring me?

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.980
Well, you were kind of sending out energy
that would make him run away.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.160
That kid is an outsider after all.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.990
We're much quicker
at detecting intruders.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.670
So far, things haven't been working out
because you've been losing your cool,

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.640
making your techniques unsuccessful.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.940
If you stay calm, we can win!

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.810
Fine! I'll keep my cool!

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:40.680
Something's here.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.580
Here it comes!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.720
Ketsu!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.160
What? My Kekkai!
What's going on?!

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.070
The floor's been gouged out!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.340
Yoshimori! It's coming back!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.140
What is that thing?!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.660
I would like to ask you something.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:27.060
Are you the Kekkaishi?

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:28.490
What if I am?

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.870
Why you-!
What's he doing to school property?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.300
I'm the one that has to clean up later,
you know!

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.440
Now what?!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.420
Hey, who do you think has
to fix that later?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.020
Are you listening? Hey!

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:15.480
Yoshimori! If you dawdle,
he'll take our prey.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.510
I know!

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.750
Damn! They're so fast!

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.790
All right. I'm getting used
to its spinning speed.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.320
I can do this!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.860
Stop breaking stuff!

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.780
Whoa! Shishio actually stopped it!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:57.860
You think you've won?
I'm most at home. in mid-air!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.380
I actually led you out here!

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.160
What?

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:06.100
It seems you're not a Kekkaishi.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.320
Wait!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.290
The way the ground was cut...

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.230
Shishio! Get away from it!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.600
That thing has...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.300
Then I have no business with you.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.110
Shishio!

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:36.650
Ketsu!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:38.720
Gen-kun!

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.760
That jerk!

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.940
Gen-kun? Gen-kun!

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.180
Thank goodness.
It seems you can hear my voice.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:58.780
Hey, don't move!

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.550
It's all right.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.390
You can leave that thing
to Yoshimori.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:06.820
Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:08.750
Ketsu!

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.790
Ketsu!

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.300
I guess it was
too hard this time!

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.600
What is he trying to do?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.560
Hey!

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.510
His wounds have already healed!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:27.900
How is this possible?

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.240
Hey, Gen-kun!

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.210
Ketsu!

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:39.490
What?!

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.520
Ketsu!

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:44.760
He was just waiting for the right moment
and right amount of strength!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.320
Ketsu!

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:48.600
But...

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.430
Was he always this strong?

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.590
No I know this.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.010
He changes as the situation demands

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.500
and hones his senses as he focuses.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.240
They're rare but they exist.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.150
Guys that evolve in
the midst of battle!

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.170
Ketsu!

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:11.930
I guess I can't cast Metsu
unless I stop it from spinning first!

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.250
Hey, Shishio!
Are you all right?

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.270
You can rest a little more.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:25.200
I actually have a lot of reasons
for sending you.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.210
But I thought that
you'd get along with Yoshimori.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.070
So that's what he meant. Dammit!

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:35.250
He's just like me.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.210
It stopped attacking.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.510
Is it running around to gain strength?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:41.890
Huh?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.190
Hey! What are you doing?
This is my Kekkai!

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:49.390
You won't be able to stop it
with your skills.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:50.420
What?

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.630
It's going to get faster.

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.670
I know! You're injured,
so stay out of this.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.400
I'm most at home in mid-air!

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:02.700
I get it.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.830
But!

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:15.290
I'll just shake you off!

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:23.230
Hey, I thought he was injured.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.660
Gen-kun is Half-Ayakashi?

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:31.500
Yeah. Unlike the Specially-Talented
who are Ayakashi users,

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:36.240
Half-Ayakashi are people who
harbor Ayakashi inside of them.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:40.540
That's why physical strength
is their greatest asset.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.220
Gen-kun!

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.520
Half-Ayakashi have
two distinct characteristics.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.250
Their amazing physical strength.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:57.560
And their astounding regenerative powers.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:03.260
Hey, if he's part Ayakashi,
isn't it bad for him to be here?

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:06.330
No. If he doesn't use
his powers excessively,

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:09.000
he shouldn't be affected by
the site too much.

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.120
There is only one rule
you must adhere to.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:17.840
I still have room to spare.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.600
He seems to be using
his powers pretty excessively...

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:34.100
Maybe we should keep an eye on him.
But still, he's impressive.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.230
What do you mean?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.530
In general, most find their powers
unmanageable.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:43.640
They lose their own humanity
as their power takes control of them,

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:48.210
or they fear their powers
and never use them.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.810
Either way, they become recluses.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.450
But he's different.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:55.320
He can completely control
his Ayakashi powers.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.150
In order to reach that level.
you'd have to endure

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:00.520
backbreaking training
and extraordinary will power.

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:04.230
Because of their abnormal bodies.

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.530
Half-Ayakashi tend to be
treated like monsters.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:08.900
He must have gone through a lot.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.780
You're such a nuisance.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.710
I don't get anything for defeating you.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:21.870
It doesn't get anything?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:25.140
Shishio!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.180
Hey! What did you mean by that?!

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.720
What do you get for defeating me?!

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:36.360
You have something like
a bounty placed on you.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:41.100
This site... I'm glad they told me
about this wonderful place!

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.120
They?!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.530
If I could just stop it from
moving for one second!

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:48.670
Ketsu!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:50.800
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:54.710
Yoshimori! What are you doing?
Pull yourself together!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.180
Shut up!

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.210
I got it! It won't be able to
move freely inside the building!

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:01.980
Hey!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:05.280
Stop using my Kekkai!

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.090
Ketsu!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.260
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.400
Playtime's over!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.470
You stay down over there!

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:25.570
How's that?!

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.770
Th-This is nothing!

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.620
W-What?!

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.300
Did he use his Kekkai to
guide that Ayakashi into place

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.630
so he could push it inside?

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:48.860
Ketsu!

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:55.470
This Kekkai is nothing!
My spinning blades can just...

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:59.410
I can't spin!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:02.180
Who're "they"?!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.440
I-I don't know what
you're talking about.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.380
I just heard about the Kekkaishi
of Karasumori that...

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.120
So you don't know anything.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.660
W-Wait! I know! Let's make a deal!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.160
I'll just run along and...

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:19.550
Metsu!

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:28.430
I was faster!
I could have finished it off!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.040
And yet in that instant he...

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:32.900
He...

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.940
He used me too!

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.550
He wasn't calculating every step.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.820
It was all instinct and
on-the-fly timing.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.440
This...

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.160
This is the power of
the Legitimate Heir?

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:49.230
A bounty?

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:52.900
Yeah. It said something about
us Kekkaishi having

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:55.730
something like a bounty on our heads.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.060
I don't understand.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.640
Setting that aside,
that was a close one!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:00.570
What was?

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:04.100
Don't play dumb!
You almost killed me!

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.610
You're already dead.
That's why you're a ghost dog.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.220
I hate it when you call me that!

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:13.280
Hakubi. does that mean
they get money for defeating us?

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.620
Ayakashi shouldn't be
interested in money.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.480
Then what do they want?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.020
That would be power.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.820
But they can get that just by coming here.

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:25.570
Right. But they're after Kekkaishi.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.760
So you must be worth something
else to them.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.540
Worth something else...

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.440
Maybe it's so they can make
a name for themselves.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.400
The stronger the enemy they defeat,
the more famous they become.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:41.650
What kind of fame will they get for
beating a little runt like him?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:42.810
What did you say?!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.320
Gen-kun, did you hear anything
from the Shadow Organization?

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.440
No.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.460
He's like that.

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.590
Even if he did know something,
he'd never...

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.750
Except... that big-head said that
they don't get anything for defeating me

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.820
because I'm not a Kekkaishi.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.020
That means that there is some reward.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.060
Oh? That's odd for Gen-kun
to be so cooperative.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.970
So there's someone willing
to pay a bounty.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.300
Come to think of it.

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:10.370
the Ayakashi said that it heard
about this land from "them."

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:11.670
"Them"?

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.940
It has to be the ones after
the Karasumori Site, right?

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:22.050
I get the feeling that this is
becoming more and more of a pain.

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.080
Me too.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:26.350
Anyway, we have to fix
this place up first.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:31.490
Hey wait. You better fix up
the places you destroyed.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.660
Why are you looking at me
like that?!

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.330
Y-Yeah! This part is my fault!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:39.770
But you destroyed a bunch of stuff too!

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:40.800
Like over here.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:44.880
I can't do stuff like that.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.800
Hey!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:49.800
Wait!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.880
Even if you can't use
the Restoration Technique

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:55.380
you can still help out by clearing
the rubble or sweeping.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:56.750
You have to help us!

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:02.680
I can't...

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.160
I only know... how to destroy...

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.470
Gen-kun! Wait! Hey!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:12.730
Leave it to me.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.540
I'll catch him.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:16.810
But I won't guarantee
that he'll be in one piece.

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:17.870
Stop it!

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.710
Let him go for today.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.240
Let's do this on our own.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.440
What? Again?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:27.280
He seemed like he didn't know
what to do.

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:32.590
With time...

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.120
I think we can get along.

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.330
Hey!

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.670
That's my spot.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.610
Stop ignoring me!

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:01.920
Fine. I'm a generous man,
so I'll give you some space.

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:06.350
Hey!

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.960
That's your side.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.230
It's so small! What's with this?!

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:12.960
I can't even turn over in this space!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.970
You have as much space as a coffin.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:16.830
That's a terrible way to put it!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:18.460
Am I a mummy from Egypt now?!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.040
I'll put a curse on you!

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:23.440
Whatever... could you just shut up?

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.410
I'll shut up if you give me
half the space.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:32.750
So you're Half-Ayakashi?

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.450
Will you be okay being here
on this site?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:39.320
I've gotten plenty of warnings about that.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:42.560
If I can keep my powers under control,
it can actually help me.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:45.590
How are your wounds?

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:46.960
I'm fine.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.470
That's no fair at all!

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:54.700
No matter how tired or injured I am,
I still have to fight every day.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:58.010
I wonder how much easier it'll be
if only I had a body like yours.

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:02.440
I didn't ask for this body.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.850
But isn't it nice to be able
to fly around so fast?

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:12.550
I don't know. Not all of it is good.

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:13.850
What do you mean?

00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:18.090
You're naïve, just like I thought.

00:22:18.470 --> 00:22:21.060
What? Are you picking
a fight with me?!

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:23.000
Hey! Wait, Shishio!

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:52.560
I will take the road
I believe in anywhere

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:56.970
Wanting to protect what's
in front of my eyes

00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:01.270
The world I have yet
to know is endless

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:05.700
I know it will make
my heart dance

00:23:07.510 --> 00:23:18.190
I feel like I could fly
for the one I love

00:23:18.230 --> 00:23:26.930
Even if I search the whole world
no one could replace you

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:31.760
Not everyone has a tomorrow

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:40.370
Don't cry

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:49.120
Even if I search the whole world
no one could replace you

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:53.950
We weren't born
to hurt each other

00:23:53.990 --> 00:24:02.370
Don't cry
